{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>In righteousness shall you judge your people</b> — a hint that courts sit on Mondays and Thursdays. בצדק — i.e., under the astrological sign of צדק (Jupiter), and צדק serves on the second day and on the fifth day at its beginning. <b>In righteousness shall you judge your people</b> — and adjacent to it: <b>You shall not go about as a talebearer</b> — a warning to a judge not to be soft toward this one and harsh toward that one, and not to say: I acquit and my colleagues convict."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:00.973402875Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}